Hi Igor,

Nothing gates v9 on your side, so please do not reorder anything. It is held to
let v8 collect more review rather than to wait on a measurement, and travelling
is a better use of the next ten days than my patch queue.

The more useful thing I can do with your result is take work off you. Do not
set up the vendor runtime after the 30th for this. Reading what the vendor
programs into A on RK3588 cannot separate my two explanations, because your own
run has just shown there is no floor on RK3588 with L of 0. There is nothing for
that A to be compensating, so whatever it holds says nothing about which of the
two is true on my SoC.

The measurement that does separate them is on RK3576 and it is mine to run. The
vendor's coefficient buffer is built at load time and is not in the .rknn, but
it can be dumped from a live run and I have done that before. Doing it for a
model whose output actually falls below its zero point, and asking whether the
vendor's A carries a lift or not, answers it directly. If it does, the
compensation was hiding in A. If it does not, there is an enable I have not
found. That is a board round here, not a setup on your bench.

What your result changed, and it changed the shape of the question rather than
one row of it. I had two explanations and a reason to prefer neither. You have
removed the one that was doing the most work, that the floor is a family trait
and the compensation therefore has to be hiding on every SoC. It is not a family
trait. So on RK3576 the difference between the vendor stack and mine is
something in my configuration, on silicon where the same 0x40ac expression
demonstrably does not floor the vendor. That is a much smaller place to look and
it is entirely on my side of the fence.

Thank you also for building the model to the case rather than to the shape. Bias
centered so the outputs straddle the zero point, 59 percent of the raw reference
below it, and mesa main so nothing in software could be compensating. The run
answers the question I asked instead of a nearby one, and the collapse to 0 of
56 against max(cpu, zp) is the control that says the comparison was live.

On the counts, one precision so the list is not read as more than it is. Of the
thirteen you have now covered, eight discriminate, and those eight land on five
distinct remainders modulo 32, which are 18, 20, 24, 26 and 28. Ten remainders
in the range have no data on either SoC. That is a long way from one data point
repeated, which is where 56, 88 and 120 left it, and it is not the whole space.
What it does establish is that the upstream constant computes whole on RK3588 at
every count anybody has proposed, with no channel pinned at the zero point in
any of them, which is the thing that mattered.

